msgid ":mod:`!atexit` --- Exit handlers"
msgstr ":mod:`!atexit` --- Penangan saat keluar"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`!atexit` module defines functions to register and "
"unregister :dfn:`exit handlers`: functions that are automatically executed "
"\"at exit\", that is, upon normal program termination (for instance, "
"if :func:`sys.exit` is called or the main module's execution completes) or, "
"more generally, upon :term:`interpreter shutdown`."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`!atexit` mendefinisikan fungsi untuk mendaftarkan dan "
"membatalkan pendaftaran :dfn:`penangan saat keluar`: fungsi yang dieksekusi "
"secara otomatis \"saat keluar\", yaitu, pada terminasi program yang normal "
"(misalnya, jika :func:`sys.exit` dipanggil atau eksekusi modul utama "
"selesai) atau, secara lebih umum, pada :term:`interpreter shutdown`."

msgid ""
"At exit, all registered exit handlers are called in the *reverse* order in "
"which they were registered. If you register ``A``, ``B``, and ``C``, at "
"interpreter shutdown time they will be run in the order ``C``, ``B``, ``A``. "
"The assumption is that lower level modules will normally be imported before "
"higher level modules and thus must be cleaned up later."
msgstr ""
"Saat keluar, semua penangan saat keluar yang terdaftar dipanggil dalam "
"urutan *terbalik* dari urutan pendaftarannya. Jika Anda mendaftarkan ``A``, "
"``B``, dan ``C``, pada saat interpreter shutdown penangan-penangan tersebut "
"akan dijalankan dalam urutan ``C``, ``B``, ``A``. Asumsinya adalah modul-"
"modul tingkat rendah biasanya akan diimpor sebelum modul-modul tingkat "
"tinggi sehingga harus dibersihkan belakangan."

msgid ""
"If an exception is raised during execution of an exit handler, a traceback "
"is printed (unless :exc:`SystemExit` is raised) and the exception "
"information is saved.  After all exit handlers have had a chance to run, the "
"last exception to be raised is re-raised."
msgstr ""
"Jika sebuah eksepsi dimunculkan selama eksekusi penangan saat keluar, "
"traceback dicetak (kecuali jika :exc:`SystemExit` dimunculkan) dan informasi "
"eksepsi disimpan. Setelah semua penangan saat keluar berkesempatan untuk "
"berjalan, eksepsi terakhir yang dimunculkan akan dimunculkan kembali."

msgid ""
"In programs that use multiple interpreters, each interpreter has its own "
"stack of exit handlers, which are executed when the interpreter shuts down "
"(for example, with :meth:`concurrent.interpreters.Interpreter.close` or the "
"C API :c:func:`Py_EndInterpreter`). Registration functions in this module "
"only affect the interpreter they are called from."
msgstr ""
"Dalam program yang menggunakan banyak interpreter, setiap interpreter "
"memiliki tumpukan penangan saat keluarnya sendiri, yang dieksekusi ketika "
"interpreter tersebut dimatikan (misalnya, "
"dengan :meth:`concurrent.interpreters.Interpreter.close` atau C "
"API :c:func:`Py_EndInterpreter`). Fungsi-fungsi pendaftaran dalam modul ini "
"hanya memengaruhi interpreter tempat fungsi-fungsi tersebut dipanggil."

msgid ""
"**Note:** Exit handlers are not called when the program is killed by a "
"signal not handled by Python, when a Python fatal internal error is "
"detected, or when :func:`os._exit` is called."
msgstr ""
"**Catatan:** Penangan saat keluar tidak dipanggil ketika program dimatikan "
"oleh sinyal yang tidak ditangani oleh Python, ketika galat internal fatal "
"Python terdeteksi, atau ketika :func:`os._exit` dipanggil."

msgid ""
"**Note:** The effect of registering or unregistering functions from within a "
"cleanup function is undefined."
msgstr ""
"**Catatan:** Efek dari mendaftarkan atau membatalkan pendaftaran fungsi dari "
"dalam sebuah fungsi cleanup tidak terdefinisi."

msgid ""
"When writing exit handlers, especially in C API extensions, keep in mind "
"that other exit handlers may still run arbitrary Python code after you clean "
"up. Such code should succeed or fail with an exception, rather than crash."
msgstr ""
"Saat menulis penangan saat keluar, terutama dalam ekstensi C API, perlu "
"diingat bahwa penangan saat keluar lain mungkin masih menjalankan kode "
"Python sembarang setelah Anda melakukan cleanup. Kode seperti itu harus "
"berhasil atau gagal dengan sebuah eksepsi, bukan crash."

msgid ""
"Attempts to start a new thread or :func:`os.fork` a new process in an exit "
"handler now leads to :exc:`RuntimeError`. Previously, this could cause race "
"conditions between the main Python runtime thread freeing thread states "
"while internal :mod:`threading` routines or the new process try to use that "
"state, which could lead to crashes rather than clean shutdown."
msgstr ""
"Upaya untuk memulai thread baru atau melakukan :func:`os.fork` terhadap "
"proses baru dalam penangan saat keluar kini menyebabkan :exc:`RuntimeError`. "
"Sebelumnya, hal ini dapat menyebabkan kondisi balapan antara thread runtime "
"Python utama yang membebaskan state thread sementara rutinitas "
"internal :mod:`threading` atau proses baru mencoba menggunakan state "
"tersebut, yang dapat menyebabkan crash alih-alih shutdown yang bersih."

msgid ""
"When used with subinterpreters, registered functions are local to the "
"interpreter they were registered in."
msgstr ""
"Ketika digunakan dengan subinterpreter, fungsi-fungsi yang terdaftar "
"bersifat lokal terhadap interpreter tempat fungsi-fungsi tersebut "
"didaftarkan."

msgid ""
"Register *func* as an exit handler. Any optional arguments that are to be "
"passed to *func* must be passed as arguments to :func:`register`. It is "
"possible to register the same function and arguments more than once."
msgstr ""
"Mendaftarkan *func* sebagai penangan saat keluar. Argumen opsional apa pun "
"yang akan diteruskan ke *func* harus diteruskan sebagai argumen "
"ke :func:`register`. Fungsi dan argumen yang sama dapat didaftarkan lebih "
"dari satu kali."

msgid ""
"This function returns *func*, which makes it possible to use it as a "
"decorator."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi ini mengembalikan *func*, yang memungkinkannya digunakan sebagai "
"dekorator."

msgid ""
"Remove *func* from the list of exit handlers. :func:`unregister` silently "
"does nothing if *func* was not previously registered.  If *func* has been "
"registered more than once, every occurrence of that function in the :mod:`!"
"atexit` call stack will be removed.  Equality comparisons (``==``) are used "
"internally during unregistration, so function references do not need to have "
"matching identities."
msgstr ""
"Menghapus *func* dari daftar penangan saat keluar. :func:`unregister` diam-"
"diam tidak melakukan apa-apa jika *func* belum pernah didaftarkan "
"sebelumnya. Jika *func* telah didaftarkan lebih dari satu kali, setiap "
"kemunculan fungsi tersebut dalam tumpukan pemanggilan :mod:`!atexit` akan "
"dihapus. Perbandingan kesetaraan (``==``) digunakan secara internal selama "
"pembatalan pendaftaran, sehingga referensi fungsi tidak perlu memiliki "
"identitas yang cocok."

msgid "Module :mod:`readline`"
msgstr "Modul :mod:`readline`"

msgid ""
"Useful example of :mod:`!atexit` to read and write :mod:`readline` history "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Contoh yang berguna dari :mod:`!atexit` untuk membaca dan menulis berkas "
"riwayat :mod:`readline`."

msgid ":mod:`!atexit` Example"
msgstr "Contoh :mod:`!atexit`"

msgid ""
"The following simple example demonstrates how a module can initialize a "
"counter from a file when it is imported and save the counter's updated value "
"automatically when the program terminates without relying on the application "
"making an explicit call into this module at termination. ::"
msgstr ""
"Contoh sederhana berikut menunjukkan bagaimana sebuah modul dapat "
"menginisialisasi sebuah pencacah dari sebuah berkas ketika modul tersebut "
"diimpor dan menyimpan nilai pencacah yang telah diperbarui secara otomatis "
"ketika program berakhir tanpa mengandalkan aplikasi untuk melakukan "
"pemanggilan eksplisit ke modul ini saat terminasi. ::"

msgid ""
"try:\n"
"    with open('counterfile') as infile:\n"
"        _count = int(infile.read())\n"
"except FileNotFoundError:\n"
"    _count = 0\n"
"\n"
"def incrcounter(n):\n"
"    global _count\n"
"    _count = _count + n\n"
"\n"
"def savecounter():\n"
"    with open('counterfile', 'w') as outfile:\n"
"        outfile.write('%d' % _count)\n"
"\n"
"import atexit\n"
"\n"
"atexit.register(savecounter)"
msgstr ""
"try:\n"
"    with open('counterfile') as infile:\n"
"        _count = int(infile.read())\n"
"except FileNotFoundError:\n"
"    _count = 0\n"
"\n"
"def incrcounter(n):\n"
"    global _count\n"
"    _count = _count + n\n"
"\n"
"def savecounter():\n"
"    with open('counterfile', 'w') as outfile:\n"
"        outfile.write('%d' % _count)\n"
"\n"
"import atexit\n"
"\n"
"atexit.register(savecounter)"

msgid ""
"Positional and keyword arguments may also be passed to :func:`register` to "
"be passed along to the registered function when it is called::"
msgstr ""
"Argumen posisional dan kata kunci juga dapat diteruskan ke :func:`register` "
"untuk diteruskan ke fungsi yang terdaftar ketika fungsi tersebut dipanggil::"

msgid ""
"def goodbye(name, adjective):\n"
"    print('Goodbye %s, it was %s to meet you.' % (name, adjective))\n"
"\n"
"import atexit\n"
"\n"
"atexit.register(goodbye, 'Donny', 'nice')\n"
"# or:\n"
"atexit.register(goodbye, adjective='nice', name='Donny')"
msgstr ""
"def goodbye(name, adjective):\n"
"    print('Goodbye %s, it was %s to meet you.' % (name, adjective))\n"
"\n"
"import atexit\n"
"\n"
"atexit.register(goodbye, 'Donny', 'nice')\n"
"# or:\n"
"atexit.register(goodbye, adjective='nice', name='Donny')"

msgid "Usage as a :term:`decorator`::"
msgstr "Penggunaan sebagai :term:`decorator`::"

msgid ""
"import atexit\n"
"\n"
"@atexit.register\n"
"def goodbye():\n"
"    print('You are now leaving the Python sector.')"
msgstr ""
"import atexit\n"
"\n"
"@atexit.register\n"
"def goodbye():\n"
"    print('You are now leaving the Python sector.')"

msgid "This only works with functions that can be called without arguments."
msgstr ""
"Hal ini hanya berfungsi dengan fungsi yang dapat dipanggil tanpa argumen."
